UNIT parse_sig
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 60b55e0a01fec765e82a808a2ede7490c1e3cf116aa0aa28046eb6dcad91682a
SIG parse_sig(s: string): { name: string, args: Array<{ name: string, type: object, rest?: true }>, result: object }
NOTE default export
ABI text = string; the result is a fresh plain object { name, args, result }; an argument is a plain object { name, type }
  plus the own property rest: true for a rest parameter only (never rest: false); a type tree is a plain object whose own
  properties are exactly k and the members the primary's DESCRIPTION names for that kind; record fields are two-element
  Arrays [name, tree]. Property order is immaterial (the canonical form sorts keys). A throw (R1, R2, R5–R8) is a thrown
  Error; the message is not graded. The artifact is an ES module default-exporting the function and imports nothing.
ENVELOPE as the primary; no widening.
MECHANISM a recursive-descent reader with one cursor over the string (index access; every accepted character is ASCII, so
  code units and code points agree): skip WHITESPACE before every token, read IDENT longest first by the IDENT pin at the
  cursor, test literal tokens with startsWith at the cursor. WHITESPACE is the four characters of the primary pin only —
  NOT the regex class \s and NOT String.prototype.trim, which accept no-break space, zero width no-break space, the line
  separator, vertical tab and form feed (all in the oracle as throws). PREFIX (R2): remember the cursor, read the prefix
  words as IDENT tokens, and keep them only when each matches and WHITESPACE then an IDENT start follow; else restore the
  cursor. Unreachable alternatives (R5): SAME compares an order-free key of each tree (union alts and record "name=key"
  fields each sorted, then joined inside brackets; tuple, list, map members in order) — NOT JSON.stringify of the tree,
  which is order-sensitive; JSON is a recursive predicate over TABLE JSON_SHAPED;
  COVERS is a recursive predicate that holds when ANY row of TABLE COVERS holds (try them all: the LIST, TUPLE, MAP
  and RECORD rows recurse into COVERS, the union rows recurse both ways); test each later alt against every earlier one.
  Nesting (R8): one depth counter, incremented on entering a composite and decremented on its closing
  bracket; recursion stays far under the default stack at 16. After the result TYPE skip WHITESPACE and require the end
  of the string. No comment stripping.
DEPENDS-ON none
PINNED regex IDENT = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/ CITED primary IDENT — applied to the remainder at the cursor
PROVENANCE rederive@bb8ded84fa50 cli/sir/canon.mjs parseSig + reader. Round 5: re-cut after FINDINGS #74 #78 #79.
